# DocGen — Final Sitagliptin Red-Flag Fix (EI + RS), Product-Agnostic

Every item below was traced against the LIVE code (`ei_core.py`, `annexure_converter.py`, `residual_solvent.py`, `residual_solvent_annexure_converter.py`, `annexure_identity_clustering.py`) and against the REAL Sitagliptin source documents (IFF PRDS, Evonik Aerosil declarations, Fujicalin statement, Olon Trilaciclib API spec). Nothing here is a guess dressed as a fix — every item states the confirmed root cause, the exact function, why it is safe for every OTHER product, and what to verify before closing it. Where the trail did not reach a confirmed cause, that is stated explicitly and a diagnostic step is given instead of a blind patch.

**Non-negotiable for every item:** the fix must be decided by WHERE a piece of evidence came from (a column label, a section heading, a document structure) — never by comparing a VALUE to a known constant (an ICH limit, a USP limit, a round number). Value-based heuristics are what caused the Trila/Vaso whack-a-mole earlier in this project; provenance-based rules are what actually generalizes across products.

