### A5. EI annexure list/narrative shows one material twice (e.g. Asahi CEOLUS + IFF MCC both appearing as separate rows/paragraphs for one composition ingredient)

**Confirmed root cause.** `assemble_and_generate`'s `annexure_list` and `generate_text_sections`'s `material_directory` both iterate over ALL of `annexure_data` unconditionally, with no filter to annexures actually selected by the matcher (`calc_tables["_match_audit"]`). RS already solves this exact problem in `residual_solvent.build_rs_payload` (the "unreferenced annexures" scoping, with a fallback that never empties the list if nothing matched at all) — EI never received the equivalent fix.

**Fix — mirror RS's existing, working mechanism exactly:**
1. Build the set of annexures actually used: every distinct `matched_key` in `calc_tables["_match_audit"]` where `matched=True`.
2. Filter `annexure_list` (in `assemble_and_generate`) and `material_directory` (in `generate_text_sections`) to only annexures whose `material_name` (or one of `_ei_material_scopes(ann)`) is in that used-set.
3. Guard: if the used-set is empty (e.g. every ingredient unmatched), fall back to showing ALL uploaded annexures — exactly mirroring RS's existing `if _mapped:` guard — so a totally-unmatched run still shows what was uploaded, never an empty list.
4. This is a display/scoping filter applied strictly AFTER matching completes. Do not touch `_resolve_ingredient_match`, `BRAND_IDENTITY_RULES`, or any scoring logic.

**Why this cannot break other products.** A document set where every uploaded annexure IS used (the common case — one annexure per composition ingredient) is unaffected, since the used-set equals the full set and the filter is a no-op. This only changes behavior when an uploaded annexure was never selected by the matcher, which by definition means it was not contributing to any calculation anyway — only its redundant DISPLAY is removed.

**Verify:** Sitagliptin EI's annexure list/narrative shows MCC once (via the IFF source, the one actually used), not twice. Any single-annexure-per-ingredient product's annexure list is byte-identical to before.

